Correct the source implementation.

## MP4 assembly

* Never concatenate MP4 binary files directly.
* Normalize source streams.
* Normalize timestamps.
* Normalize frame rates.
* Normalize pixel formats.
* Normalize audio sample rates.
* Use correct FFmpeg concat workflows.
* Generate to temporary files.
* Validate the result.
* Publish atomically.

## Mandatory quality control

Use FFprobe and complete FFmpeg decoding.

Test:

* Container integrity.
* Duplicate MOOV atoms.
* Invalid NAL units.
* Corrupt frames.
* Missing frames.
* Unexpected black frames.
* Frozen intervals.
* Video duration.
* Audio duration.
* Resolution.
* Frame rate.
* Audio coverage.
* Synchronization.
* Download integrity.

Use full decoding tests, including:

`ffmpeg -v error -i input.mp4 -f null -`

Capture the actual exit code and diagnostic output.

A corrupted master must never receive COMPLETED status.

